WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.268
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.669
We're here with
Christine Baranski, everybody,

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:06.105
and we're so happy to have you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:10.276
So, the Diane Lockhart saga,
as we --

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.978
I mean, again,
she's had two shows.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.413
You know, she went
from "The Good Wife"

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:16.515
to "The Good Fight."
But I heard you were surprised

00:00:16.515 --> 00:00:18.852
to find out that the sixth
would be the final season.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:24.457
-Probably because I had --
I had such a happy day at work.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:29.495
I was literally in bed between
John Slattery and Gary Cole

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:31.897
in a kind of fantasy sequence,
and I'm thinking,

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:35.969
"Who has my life -- at any age,
much less my age?"

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:41.073
And it was such a happy workday,
and you know, so to be told --

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:42.608
But I don't think
you're ever ready

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:45.811
to hear that something
that you've done for 13 years

00:00:45.811 --> 00:00:49.081
with a family of people
with whom you've --

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.650
some of them
I had known for 13 years --

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.186
my costume designer,
my makeup artist,

00:00:54.186 --> 00:00:55.755
some of the cameramen.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:58.324
I mean, 13 years,
that's your family.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:02.161
You go from like, you know,
their kids are little,

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:03.963
and then they're
applying for college.

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:07.833
And you live your whole life
with these people.

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:12.305
And so, no, I wasn't -- I still
don't think I've processed it,

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.040
'cause I just went
right into "Gilded Age."

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.910
I think when -- probably
after the first of the year,

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.113
when we would have gone back,
it's going to be like, "Whoa."

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:24.216
Because, you know, people
really get very close,

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:29.088
and it's not the same
as with your "family" family.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.390
You know, the Teamster
is not going to say,

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.059
"Well, what about the weekend.
You didn't call."

00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:37.863
Or the cameraman is not going to
say, "I can hear

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:39.665
from your tone of voice,
you're upset."

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:41.067
-Yeah.
-And you know, they --

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.936
People in
a professional situation,

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.105
there's a protocol and a clarity
to it,

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:49.808
and it's a wonderful family.
I will miss everybody.

00:01:49.808 --> 00:01:53.646
I will miss my fellow actors,
my crew, my producers.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.581
It was a great show.
It was a great run.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:58.184
And it was six years
on "The Good Fight."

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:01.987
And it was a show about what was
happening in this Trump era.

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:03.189
I was listening
to your monologue.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.857
You do a great Donald Trump,
by the way.

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:06.192
-Thank you very much.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.595
We're very similar.
I think that helps.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.229
[ Laughter ]
-But, I mean, all that vent --

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:11.897
You get to vent in your job.
-Yes.

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:14.534
-And I used to vent as Diane,
because it --

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:18.103
she was living through the Trump
era as a liberal feminist.

00:02:18.103 --> 00:02:21.608
So, I'll also miss
not being Diane,

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:24.576
and taking my anxieties
and anger to work.

00:02:24.576 --> 00:02:26.545
I mean, what would you do
if you didn't have this show?

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:27.847
Your poor wife would --
-You just mutter to yourself

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.582
on the street, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.617
-You take it, you know,
to your kids.

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:33.519
-It's the hardest thing
about having a month off,

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.121
is, you know --
-I could tell.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:37.123
You were so pent-up.
-I was so happy, yeah.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.191
'Cause they don't let me do
"A Closer Look" at home,

00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:41.527
because I have three kids,
and two of them are

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.530
Trump supporters, yeah.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.034
The 6-year-old and the baby,
yeah.

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.635
-And the baby.
-The baby, yeah.

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:52.138
It's just -- It's a tax thing.
For her, it's just about taxes.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.540
-Typical Republican baby.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.076
-Whining all the time.
-They are very whiny.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.745
[ Laughs ]
But the other thing --

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:02.114
and I think it's really
important that you stress --

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:04.583
and I certainly felt it here
during the pandemic --

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:06.953
when you're away, like,
the comfort of having a crew

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.787
that takes care of you
behind the scenes

00:03:08.787 --> 00:03:10.622
is just a wonderful --
-Incredible.

00:03:10.622 --> 00:03:12.825
All those years, because we were
shooting the pilot

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:15.762
on election night --
so "The Good Fight" took us

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:18.765
all through the Trump years, and
would that they had been over,

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:21.700
but it seems the post-Trump
years are equally...

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.202
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:26.639
-And so, it was a place to go.
So, there was Trump

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.209
and there's COVID,
and we were still

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.977
a functioning group of people.
It was --

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:34.614
Even when it was hard,
we all got through it.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:37.316
I don't remember people
complaining, and, you know --

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:39.418
So, when they announced the end,
it wasn't like,

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:41.921
"Oh, well, of course. Thank God.
You know, we're tired,

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.623
and we just keep repeating
the same stories."

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.390
This show
just kept staying fresh.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.560
-It was very --
I mean, you know,

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.897
to write an episodic drama
as topical as you guys were,

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.698
not a lot of people do it.
-There was always bad news.

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:54.266
It's like your show.
-Right, yeah.

00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:56.702
-There's always bad news,
so you always have raw material.

00:03:56.702 --> 00:04:00.139
But I will miss it, and I'll --
I will also say,

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:03.509
we had just a revolving door
on great actors

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:05.344
who would come in
and do guest appearances,

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:06.912
'cause we'd have
all the New York actors.

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:08.280
-You had
all the New York actors.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.083
And this season, John Slattery
showed up in the clip.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:12.485
Andre Braugher.
I mean, it really is --

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.787
-Carrie Preston.
Alan Cumming makes a --

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.823
a comeback, and no pun intended.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:19.926
He Cummings back.
-He Cummings back, yeah.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:23.395
-You know, I will miss
every aspect of it.

00:04:23.395 --> 00:04:25.964
But, you know, I think,
narratively speaking,

00:04:25.964 --> 00:04:28.601
it was the time.
You know, you don't want to

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.236
keep a show on
when you start repeating.

00:04:31.236 --> 00:04:34.440
Like, repeating jokes or
repeating dramatic things.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.744
Diane's anger and
her exasperation

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:40.212
took her to such a point
that she was literally

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:44.349
using hallucinogens or whatever,
and levitating.

00:04:44.349 --> 00:04:45.785
I mean, where do you go
after you levitate...

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.787
-Yeah, it's hard.
-...to cope with anxiety.

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.288
-Yeah, it's very hard
to bounce back from that.

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:52.692
The good news is, now you have
an open slot on your schedule,

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:54.861
you have committed to doing
my Broadway musical,

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:56.261
"Cicada, Cicada."
-Yes.

00:04:56.261 --> 00:04:58.030
-And we're very --
-Which needs a lot of work.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.832
-What?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:03.435
You don't -- You don't
love the script so far?

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:07.306
-It's hard to -- you know,
you talk about character work.

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.742
Well, playing an insect,
you know.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:14.013
And then, it's just --
and a musical of an insect.

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.481
You know?
-Yeah.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:18.350
-But I think it's gonna go out
of town for a very long time.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:22.154
[ Laughter ]
-That is so sweet of you to say.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:24.857
[ Laughter ]
Well, we are just so happy

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:27.459
every time you're here,
and congratulations

00:05:27.459 --> 00:05:29.529
on an incredible run
with an incredible character.

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:30.897
-Than you.
-Christine Baranski, everybody.

